<header>
    <h1>Computer Hardware Evaluation</h1>
    <p>Understanding the most important computer components</p>
</header>

<section>
    <h2>Introduction</h2>
    <p>
        Computer hardware is made up of physical parts that allow a computer
        to operate. Each component has a different job, but they all work
        together to make a computer run smoothly. Four important components
        are the CPU, RAM, SSD, and GPU.
    </p>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Hardware Comparison Table</h2>

    <table>
        <tr>
            <th>Component</th>
            <th>Description</th>
            <th>Importance</th>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>CPU</td>
            <td>The Central Processing Unit is the brain of the computer.
            It processes instructions and performs calculations.</td>
            <td>It is important because it controls tasks and helps
            programs run.</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>RAM</td>
            <td>Random Access Memory temporarily stores information
            that the computer is currently using.</td>
            <td>It allows the computer to multitask and run programs
            smoothly.</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>SSD</td>
            <td>A Solid State Drive stores files, applications,
            and the operating system.</td>
            <td>It helps the computer start faster and load
            programs and files quickly.</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>GPU</td>
            <td>The Graphics Processing Unit handles images,
            videos, graphics, and visual effects.</td>
            <td>It is important for gaming, video editing,
            and other graphics-heavy tasks.</td>
        </tr>
    </table>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>CPU - Central Processing Unit</h2>
    <img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Intel_Core_i7_Logo.svg/320px-Intel_Core_i7_Logo.svg.png"
         alt="Intel CPU logo">
    <p>
        The CPU is considered the brain of the computer. It handles
        instructions and calculations. A faster CPU can help a computer
        complete tasks more efficiently.
    </p>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>RAM - Random Access Memory</h2>
    <img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/DDR4_RAM.jpg/320px-DDR4_RAM.jpg"
         alt="Computer RAM">
    <p>
        RAM temporarily holds data that the computer needs right away.
        Having more RAM can help a computer run multiple applications
        without slowing down as much.
    </p>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>SSD - Solid State Drive</h2>
    <img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/SSD_2.5_inch.jpg/320px-SSD_2.5_inch.jpg"
         alt="Solid State Drive">
    <p>
        An SSD is used to save files, games, and programs.
        It is faster than traditional hard drives because it uses
        flash memory instead of moving mechanical parts.
    </p>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>GPU - Graphics Processing Unit</h2>
    <img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Nvidia_GeForce_GTX_1080.jpg/320px-Nvidia_GeForce_GTX_1080.jpg"
         alt="Graphics card">
    <p>
        The GPU processes graphics and images. It is especially
        important for gaming, graphic design, and video editing
        because it helps display detailed visuals.
    </p>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Conclusion</h2>
    <p>
        All four hardware components play an important role in a computer.
        The CPU processes instructions, RAM helps with multitasking,
        the SSD stores information, and the GPU handles graphics.
        Together, they help a computer perform everyday tasks and
        more demanding activities.
    </p>
</section>

